course: dictionary
lesson: 2950
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «The tap has been dripping all night.» Here drip is a verb: water is falling in small drops. «A drip of water ran down the window.» Here drip is a noun: one single drop.
explain: Drip also has a medical meaning. «The patient had a drip in her arm.» The clues are patient and hospital, so a drip here is the tube that puts liquid slowly into the body. Always ask: which meaning fits these words?
explain: To check your meaning, put it into the sentence in place of the word. If «falling in small drops» makes sense in «The tap has been dripping all night», you have found the right meaning.
fact: Drip can be a verb (drip, drips, dripped, dripping) or a noun (a drip, drips).
fact: «Dripping» means falling in small drops, as in «a dripping tap».
fact: «A drip» can mean one drop of liquid, or the sound of drops.
fact: In a hospital, «a drip» puts liquid slowly into a patient's body.
fact: Water dripping from a recorder comes from warm, wet breath cooling inside the pipe and turning back into drops.
exercise: «The tap has been dripping all night.» What does dripping mean here? | Frozen solid | Running very fast in a stream | Shining brightly | *Falling in small drops
exercise: «A drip of water ran down the window.» What is a drip here? | Water in a big flood | A cold wind | A bird's song | *One drop of water
exercise: «The patient had a drip in her arm.» What does a drip do in a hospital? | *Puts liquid slowly into the body | Measures the height of a bed | Cleans the floor | Blows warm air
test: «The paint began to drip down the wall.» What does drip mean here? | *Fall in small drops | Make a loud bang | Dry quickly in the sun | Stick very firmly
test: «Water dripping from a recorder is condensation.» Where does this water come from? | *Warm, wet breath that cools inside the pipe and turns into drops | A tap left running in the kitchen | Rain falling through an open window | Sea spray blown onto the beach
exam: Which meaning fits «Each drip from the broken pipe wasted water»? | A loud shout | A large wave | A bright light | *One drop
